/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Open Seam: An open seam is one where the seam allowances on each side of the seam have been pressed open, with the wrong side of the fabric facing the wrong side. This technique creates a flat, neat finish and is commonly used in garments and sewing projects.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
